-- title:
--   Idempotent splitting of the Hecke algebra of a Hecke datum
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring which is adically complete for its maximal ideal, let $V$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-module that is finite as an $\mathcal{O}$-module, and let $k$ be a field equipped with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra structure. Let $D$ be a Hecke datum for $(\mathcal{O},V,k)$, that is: a type $D.\mathrm{Gen}$ of generator labels, a family $D.\mathrm{op}$ of $\mathcal{O}$-linear endomorphisms of $V$ indexed by it, a proof that these endomorphisms commute pairwise, and a function $D.\bar\theta$ from the labels to $k$. Write $\mathbb{T} =$ `D.opSubalgebra` for the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal{O}}(V)$ generated by the image of $D.\mathrm{op}$; by the commutation hypothesis it is a commutative ring. The assertion is that the type of idempotent splittings of $\mathbb{T}$ is nonempty, i.e. there exist an $n \in \mathbb{N}$, elements $e_0,\dots,e_{n-1} \in \mathbb{T}$ forming a complete family of orthogonal idempotents, and ideals $\mathfrak{m}_0,\dots,\mathfrak{m}_{n-1}$ of $\mathbb{T}$, each maximal, such that every maximal ideal of $\mathbb{T}$ equals some $\mathfrak{m}_i$, and $e_i \in \mathfrak{m}_j$ if and only if $i \neq j$.
--
--   This is the semilocal decomposition of a Hecke algebra acting on a finite module over a complete Noetherian local ring: such an algebra is a finite product of local rings, recorded here in the form of a complete set of orthogonal idempotents matched bijectively with the maximal ideals. It is the starting point for the localisation and corner-ring arguments used to extract eigenvectors and to analyse Hecke operators at a prime, as in [`CohCarrier.HeckeData.exists_eigenvector_H1_of_toML_ne_zero`](thm.html#CohCarrier.HeckeData.exists_eigenvector_H1_of_toML_ne_zero) and the statements about corner rings at primes.
